<title>HONG KONG: Shenzhen electronic sector '96 profit rises 25 pct.</title>
<headline>Shenzhen electronic sector '96 profit rises 25 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shenzhen's electronic industry generated pre-tax profits of 3.5 billion yuan ($421.7 million) in 1996, up 25 percent from 1995, the Shenzhen Special Zone Daily said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Sales also increased 25 percent to 50 billion yuan last year, accounting for 17 percent of the country's total, two percentage points more than 1995, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>Colour televisions, stereos and radios are the key money-makers in the industry, it said.</p>
<p>Other more high-end electronic products such as computers and optic-fibre cables showed solid growth, with their output value soaring 80 percent year-on-year in 1996, it said.</p>
<p>($1=8.3 yuan)</p>
</text>
